            "target_entity_instance": "Irish Atlantic Margin",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "As has been shown by previous studies, SLA (sea level anomaly) was found to significantly influence the presence of sperm whales (Correia et al., 2015; Davis et al., 2002; Pirotta et al., 2020; Shabangu and Andrew, 2020; Virgili et al., 2019). The trends revealed by the partial plots (Figure 3) should however be treated with caution as the clear peak observed is unlikely to have any ecological explanation, but rather be due to data distribution artefacts. SLA is a good indicator of mesoscale eddies (Pegliasco et al., 2021), features playing an important role in aggregating prey (Davis et al., 2002), which explains their association with sperm whale occurrence.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
